WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.900
I'll write. I promise.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.690
You're going back to Korea, then?

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.200
I need to look for someone before I do that.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:15.820
Yujin!

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.200
Here, I found it.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.540
Found what?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.200
This.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.870
Remember you had a cassette tape in that bag I stole?

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.830
<i>Surprised?</i>

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.810
<i>I know it's late, but I got you a Christmas present.</i>

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:41.930
<i>Merry Christmas!</i>

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.350
Who is it?

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.240
Is that the man you're looking for?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.000
Yeah.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.290
<i>How are you, Mom?</i>

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.750
<i>I hope you're not spending your days sighing and worrying about me.</i>

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.420
<i>You better not be giving Mom any trouble</i>

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.800
<i>and causing her more wrinkles, Huijin.</i>

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.680
Look who's talking.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.520
<i>I'm at the airport right now.</i>

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.020
<i>I'm heading over to New York on urgent business.</i>

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.110
<i>New York is...</i>

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.250
All right!

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.410
That's it, right there!

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.370
That's it. Yeah!

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.210
Come on, who loves her daddy?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.270
Hey, Sweetheart, can we have kimchijeon for dinner?

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.680
Nothing beats kimchijeon on a rainy day like this.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.010
What do you think?

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.770
Huh?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.860
What's wrong?

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.520
Is it from Yujin?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.070
Is something wrong?

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.070
Yujin...

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.530
Yujin...

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.810
What is it?

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.080
Tell me!

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.330
Yujin says she's in New York.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.600
Why are you crying about it?

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.000
What's so sad about her being in New York?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.880
I...

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:01.090
I barely got to go to Jeju Island for my honeymoon, but she's...

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.250
Jihyeon!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.810
Are you all right?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.800
I'm so sorry, Baby.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.310
Mommy's sorry.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.230
<i>I read in a book somewhere,</i>

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:28.530
<i>that wandering strangers feel at home in New York City,</i>

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:33.040
<i>because everything moves so fast here that one has no time</i>

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.480
<i>even to reminisce about one's past or one's home.</i>

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.140
<i>Director Minhyung Lee resigned a long time ago.</i>

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.920
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.</i>

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.900
Do you know where he might have moved to?

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.530
No idea.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.830
<i>Manager Kim apparently quit last year.</i>

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.500
<i>He changed his cell phone number, so I can't reach him either.</i>

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.080
Really?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.750
<i>What are you going to do now?</i>

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.790
<i>Why don't you come back to Korea?</i>

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.670
<i>Your old desk at the office is always ready for you.</i>

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.970
You want to start negotiating your salary now?

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.180
How much do you want?

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.700
<i>I'm fine.</i>

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.270
<i>You couldn't afford me anyway.</i>

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.230
<i>Oh, and I couldn't get a hold of Sanghyuk.</i>

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.480
<i>Did something happen to him?</i>

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.570
You <i>really</i> didn't call him even once this whole time?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.750
He moved to a different TV station.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.360
He said he was going to shoot a documentary or something.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.200
<i>I had no idea.</i>

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.700
<i>But then again, it's been a while since I talked to him.</i>

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.730
<i>I'll give you his new number.</i>

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.080
<i>Why don't you give him a call?</i>

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.050
Running camera tests.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.510
All right, why don't we check tomorrow's forecast and call it a day?

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.530
Let's call it a day here.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.220
We'll come back here early tomorrow morning.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.350
We'll finish shooting Sangwang Peak then.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.730
Thanks for all your hard work.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:23.320
Thank you.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.110
Thank you.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:27.190
Don't forget that tape.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:27.940
Yes, Director.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.570
Hey, Sanghyuk Kim!

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.410
Chelin, why are you...

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:41.940
Didn't you say this documentary was called "The Four Seasons at Mt. Odae"?

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.420
Shouldn't <i>one</i> year be enough to film all four seasons?

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.340
Why is it taking you <i>years?</i>

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.510
How'd you know I was here?

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:57.470
I called the TV station.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.180
You haven't had dinner yet, right?

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.690
You've no idea how hard it was to track you down.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:02.480
Okay, okay.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.910
Oh my God, my shoes are all wet.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:05.730
You've no idea how uncomfortable this is.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:22.310
So it's been a year since Yongguk and Jinsook got married?

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.230
Remember how they were totally putting on a show that day?

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.060
A show?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.780
Remember how quiet that wedding felt,

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.450
because neither Yujin nor Joonsang were there?

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.200
So they were both extra festive to get us in the mood too.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.580
Wouldn't you call that a show?

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.370
I see.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.000
Yujin...

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.290
I've been thinking about her a lot.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.960
I tried to contact her every time I went to France,

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.220
but, in the end, I couldn't.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.130
What about Joonsang?

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.050
It's as if he disappeared into thin air.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.180
Both he and his mother, that is.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.140
What are you talking about?

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.800
Remember Manager Kim?

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:07.060
The guy who used to work for Ms. Mi Hee.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.110
He called me to make sure I'd notify him

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:15.990
if I somehow got a hold of Joonsang or Ms. Mi Hee.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.230
<i>Yujin...</i>

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.190
<i>Why are you smiling?</i>

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.490
<i>This reminded me of my Mom and Dad.</i>

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.700
<i>They apparently used to walk around like this when they were dating.</i>

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.370
<i>They'd just walk?</i>

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.160
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.450
<i>Neither of them had any money back then,</i>

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.460
<i>and they didn't want to go back to their homes,</i>

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.790
<i>so supposedly they just walked around the neighborhood like this.</i>

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.130
<i>If you count all the times they walked,</i>

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.460
<i>they probably walked around the world about ten times.</i>

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.140
<i>What was your father like?</i>

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:24.720
<i>Yujin!</i>

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.430
<i>Joonsang!</i>

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.200
Are you sure it exists?

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.030
Yeah, I swear!

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.830
You'll be surprised when you see it.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.290
Trust me.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.210
Are you sure you saw it?

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.840
Of course I did.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:01.640
Really?

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.640
Yeah.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.760
It's a bench with a star necklace embedded in it instead of a message.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.350
Where is it?

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.680
We've been looking for it for a whole hour now.

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:14.440
Everyone's going to call us liars if we don't find that bench.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.930
I told you the bench grants wishes to those who find it, didn't I?

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.150
Trust me on this one.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.200
It was around here somewhere...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:21.490
Is it this one?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:23.450
No...

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.450
Not this one?

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:26.640
I found it!

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:27.740
It's here!

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:28.330
What did I tell you?

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.500
It <i>does</i> exist.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.790
It's so pretty.

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:40.010
<i>From now on, look for Polaris whenever you get lost.</i>

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.470
<i>Polaris never changes.</i>

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:47.510
<i>It always stays in the same place, regardless of the season.</i>

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.030
Joonsang...

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:04.950
Yujin?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.190
You're Yujin, right?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.850
This way, please.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.140
Let's play shadow puppets.

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:41.400
Now watch.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:46.610
Hey, look!

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.410
It's so cute!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:50.700
Do something else.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.830
A man went to the Kingdom of Shadows...

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.250
<i>Hey, Yujin,</i>

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.340
<i>have you heard the story about the Kingdom of Shadows?</i>

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.050
A man went to the Kingdom of Shadows,

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.470
<i>but no one would talk to him because they were all shadows.</i>

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:13.480
So he was lonely there all by himself.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:22.650
<i>And that's the end of it.</i>

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:30.870
<i>Do you know how not to feel lonely in the Kingdom of Shadows?</i>

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.880
<i>You just need to have someone remember your shadow.</i>

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.500
<i>Like this.</i>

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.260
I had no idea.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:55.330
I had no idea Joonsang's illness was so serious,

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.060
or that he'd had surgery for it.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.770
I really had no idea.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.360
It probably would have been harder for Minhyung if you had known.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:09.110
Oh... I guess I should be calling him "Joonsang" now.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:14.330
I told you that we used to be old friends, right?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.680
I bet he was the first one to tell you the story

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.880
about the Kingdom of Shadows.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.880
How did his operation turn out?

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:33.180
Joonsang is all right, isn't he?

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.560
Do you see the blue dot?

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.730
Focus.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:49.610
You need to tell me whether you see it or not.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.370
Do you see it?

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.840
Let's give it another try.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.640
Do you see a rod or a balloon?

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.390
Anything at all.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:19.090
Even if everything's blurry,

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:21.690
it means the problem isn't your depth perception or field of vision.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:24.810
It's a sign that your optic nerves are recovering.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:27.570
What if I can't see a thing?

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.810
We'll have to give it some time.

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:33.870
We've removed the hematoma for now, so...

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.610
I guess I should give up on my eyes,

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:40.250
because I scraped through with my life.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.420
Don't say it like that!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.500
It's only fair.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.040
You gain one...

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.590
you lose another.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:05.560
Minhyung!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.690
Are you all right?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.620
It's only been a month since your operation.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.460
We need to give it some time.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.340
I'm not asking you as my doctor,

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.480
but as my friend.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.090
Be honest.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:36.950
We operated on him too late

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:38.600
to reverse the damage to his optic nerves.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.930
It's a miracle that some of his optic nerves

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.440
are still intact.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.100
But I...

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:52.030
had no idea how much pain he was in.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.530
I see.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.990
He wasn't hurting just because he had lost his eyesight,

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:03.410
but also because he knew that he couldn't go back to you without his eyes.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:06.460
That's why he was in pain.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.210
And so was Ms. Mi Hee, who stood by his side watching.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:14.800
She kept blaming herself,

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.110
saying that because she lied,

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:18.800
Joonsang had lost his vision and you.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.220
She lied?

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:25.980
I thought she lied, saying that you two had the same father?

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:27.850
What do you mean, "she lied"?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.410
Are you sure you're not mistaken?

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.230
We're...

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:34.240
brother and sister.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.240
You mean you didn't know this whole time?

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.540
You and Joonsang are not related.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.080
Joonsang's father is...

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.760
Remember I told you about my college reunion next week?

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.620
I forgot to mention this earlier,

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.890
but they want us to bring our spouses this year.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.480
So prepare accordingly.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.640
What do I have to prepare?

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.640
Hello?

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:12.690
You found them?

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.030
Please hold on.

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:17.720
Yes.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.240
Oh, I see.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.720
Your soup must be cold.

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:34.800
Should I reheat it for you?

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.210
Would you?

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.340
Oh no, just leave it.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.140
So then they found Joonsang?

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.520
Or is it Ms. Mi Hee they found?

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.560
How did you...

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.560
Ms. Mi Hee and I may not share the best of relationships,

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:55.400
but Joonsang is your offspring.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.680
Go.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:18:59.860
Go see her.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.530
H-Honey...

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:06.620
Honey.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.920
You said you were an only child, right?

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:22.260
Couldn't you tell that I was a little princess from the get-go?

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:24.180
I guess.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.930
Have you ever wished you had a brother or sister?

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:29.680
Maybe.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:34.400
I guess I wouldn't mind a younger brother who's like you.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.230
A younger, but not an older, brother?

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.030
Why are you asking all of a sudden?

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.460
Are you angry?

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:56.690
Fine, fine.

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:57.780
An "older brother" like you.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:58.750
You happy now?

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.340
Joonsang...

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.220
is actually my brother.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.600
He's not related to Yujin in any way.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:08.170
He's <i>my</i> father's son.

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:09.140
He's <i>my</i> brother.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:20.440
Does Yujin know about this?

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:23.910
Then...

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.250
Why...

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:35.420
Why...

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.130
didn't he tell me?

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:40.710
I would never have left him if he had.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.430
I would've stayed with him until the end,

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.930
no matter how much he ran or pushed me away.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:16.120
Get out of there.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.000
What are you doing?

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:19.210
It's you, Jane.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.840
I'm doing what you told me.

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.590
I may not be able to see it, but you see it, don't you?

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:29.640
Can't you see the waters shaking?

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:31.680
That means the Angel of Bethesda is here right now.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.140
Minhyung!

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.540
You said it can cure <i>any</i> disease, right?

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:37.270
Then it should be able to cure my eyes too.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.770
Don't be like this!

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.360
What I need now is a miracle.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:45.320
You know that.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.460
Where's Joonsang now?

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:00.150
I don't care!

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.590
I don't care if he can see or not!

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:05.050
I can see him right now, can't I?

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:25.940
You couldn't tell Yujin because you still have feelings for her, right?

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:29.910
Would you be able to tell her if you were in my shoes?

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:34.370
I would have.

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:40.790
I really don't know what I can do to help either of them.

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:43.750
I still don't.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.110
What about you?

00:22:45.110 --> 00:22:46.840
Are <i>you</i> okay with all this?

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:51.010
Ever since the day I thought Joonsang had died...

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:54.100
For ten years I wanted to become Joonsang.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:58.340
I thought I could be with Yujin without hurting her

00:22:58.340 --> 00:23:00.480
and without letting her suffer that way.

00:23:01.850 --> 00:23:04.160
I hated Joonsang so much that I wanted to kill him

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:06.360
when he reappeared in front of me.

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:11.360
I thought, "Why did he have to show up <i>now</i>?"

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.740
Sorry, I shouldn't have brought him to you guys.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.210
To think that the Joonsang I hated so much is my own brother...

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:26.630
and that he's dying, even as we speak.

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:33.660
If he doesn't give me a chance to apologize for all that's happened,

00:23:34.550 --> 00:23:37.390
I really won't be able to forgive him this time.
